    <!-- 06 Brief Structure -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="briefing">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">06 &mdash; Briefing</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">How to brief for whitelabel UGC</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brief = product + messaging + hooks + tone + format + do's and don'ts</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Give talking points, not a word-for-word script</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Include reference videos &mdash; "like this, for our product"</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The whitelabel UGC brief template</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Product details.</strong> What the product is, what it does, key features, and who it's for. Include a product sample or free access so the creator can actually use it. Authentic experience makes better content.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Key messages.</strong> 2&ndash;3 talking points the creator must cover. Not a script &mdash; bullet points they can express naturally. "Mention the 30-day guarantee." "Show the before and after." "Reference how long it took to see results."</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Hooks.</strong> Provide 3&ndash;5 hook options for the creator to choose from (or use as inspiration). Specific hooks: "I tried every productivity app and this is the only one that stuck." Generic hooks that don't work: "Check out this amazing product."</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Tone and style.</strong> Describe the energy: casual, energetic, calm, authoritative. Link 2&ndash;3 reference videos that show the style you want. "Like creator X's video about product Y, but for our product."</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Format specifications.</strong> Vertical 9:16. Duration (15&ndash;45s recommended). Ad type (testimonial, demo, unboxing, before/after). Whether face-to-camera, product-only, or mixed.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Do's and don'ts.</strong> What to avoid: competitor mentions, medical/legal claims, showing competing products. What to include: product name (with correct pronunciation), specific CTA language, any required disclosures.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Briefing for remix potential</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Since whitelabel UGC will be edited by the brand's team, brief creators to deliver "modular" content. Ask for: the full video as scripted, plus 2&ndash;3 alternate hook openings filmed separately. This gives the brand's media team raw material to assemble multiple ad variants without re-contacting the creator. One delivery becomes three or four testable ads.</p>

        <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6 my-6 flex gap-4 items-start flex-col sm:flex-row">
