        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">07 &mdash; Quality</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Quality control and revisions</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">1&ndash;2 revision rounds are standard (included in price)</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Review against the brief, not against subjective preference</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brand guidelines must be provided upfront, not after delivery</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The quality review process</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Check against the brief.</strong> Did the creator hit all the talking points? Is the hook clear? Is the product shown correctly? Is the duration within spec? Review objectively against the brief, not subjectively against personal taste.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Technical quality.</strong> Audio must be clear (no background noise, echo, or muffled voice). Lighting must be adequate (face visible, product visible). Video must be in focus and vertical. These are non-negotiable minimums.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Authenticity check.</strong> Does the content feel natural? Over-rehearsed delivery kills the UGC advantage. The slight imperfections &mdash; natural pauses, casual language &mdash; are features, not bugs. Don't ask for re-takes that make the content feel scripted.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Revision requests.</strong> If revisions are needed, provide specific, actionable feedback. "Re-record the hook using option 3 from the brief" is good. "Make it feel more energetic" is vague and leads to frustration. Limit revisions to 1&ndash;2 rounds &mdash; if the brief was clear, most content should be usable on the first take.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Approval workflow</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Keep the approval chain short. The person reviewing the content should be the same person who wrote the brief. Adding multiple reviewers with different opinions leads to conflicting feedback, unnecessary revisions, and content that loses its authentic feel. One reviewer, one set of feedback, one round of revisions.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

