    <!-- 09 Common Mistakes -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="mistakes">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; Mistakes</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Common mistakes with whitelabel UGC</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Ordering too few videos = not enough data to find winners</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Over-editing raw files = destroying the authentic UGC feel</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Vague briefs = generic content that doesn't convert</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Ordering too few videos.</strong> Commissioning 2&ndash;3 whitelabel videos and hoping for a winner. The realistic hit rate is 10&ndash;20%. You need at least 10 videos per testing cycle to generate reliable learning. Think in batches, not singles.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Over-editing the raw files.</strong> Adding brand intros, motion graphics, cinematic color grading, or music beds that make the content feel produced. The whole value of whitelabel UGC is that it looks authentic. Add captions. Don't add a studio finish.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Vague briefs.</strong> Sending the creator a one-line brief like "Talk about how much you like the product." This produces generic content that doesn't convert. Invest in specific briefs with concrete hooks, clear talking points, and reference videos.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Not requesting modular hooks.</strong> Only asking for one version of the video. Always request 2&ndash;3 alternate hook openings. Hooks are the biggest lever in ad performance, and testing multiple hooks per body content multiplies your testing capacity at minimal additional cost.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Treating production as a one-time project.</strong> Ordering one batch of whitelabel UGC and expecting it to work for months. Creative fatigue is real &mdash; winning ads degrade after 2&ndash;4 weeks. Plan for ongoing monthly production.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Ignoring performance data.</strong> Not tracking which creators, hooks, and ad types performed best. Every batch should inform the next. If testimonial ads from female creators aged 25&ndash;34 consistently outperform demo ads, your next batch should skew toward more of what works.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

